      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_007",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_007",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.2 Missing data",
      "text": "%md\n## 2.2 Missing data\n\nA blank (null) cell can mean \"not recorded\", \"not applicable\" or \"unchanged\". For each column the table gives the\nshare of rows that are blank, and for numbers the share that are zero or less. The last column says what a blank\nmeans for the model and what the model does with it. The next two tables check whether blanks are getting more or\nless common over time, and test our reading of the most important blank, the original tax (E08).",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_008",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_008",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.2 Missing data",
      "text": "%pyspark\nBLANK_MEANS = {'taxpayer_tin': 'No taxpayer: the row is dropped (R1, E03)',\n               'entry_num': 'No entry number: the declaration ID is used as the entry key',\n               'clearance_station_cd': 'No station: counted as a station of its own in the station measures',\n               'dec_ref_yer': 'No year: the declaration ID is used as the entry key',\n               'decl_status': 'No status: the row is dropped with the cancelled ones (R3)',\n               'regime_cd': 'No regime: the row is dropped (R4)',\n               'hsc_cd': 'No tariff code: no price or duty benchmark for the item; it still counts in its declaration',\n               'gds_org_cty': 'No origin: the item is compared with the benchmark for its HS code across all origins',\n               'cpc_cd': 'No APC: not counted as exempt, and left out of the duty comparison (that uses APC 000 only)',\n               'customs_value': 'No value: left out of the price, duty and APC features (E11)',\n               'net_weight': 'No weight: left out of the price features (E11)',\n               'supplementary_qnty': 'No units: the price is compared per kg only',\n               'tax_assessed': 'No item tax: left out of the duty features',\n               'original_tax_amt': 'Read as unchanged: the final tax is used (E08)',\n               'final_amt': 'No final tax: no top-up or tax reduction can be counted',\n               'top_up_amt': 'Not used by the model (E09)',\n               'top_up_flg': 'Read as no top-up',\n               'amendment_flg': 'Read as not amended',\n               'pay_status': 'Read as not unpaid',\n               'preferential_treatment_flag': 'Read as no preference claimed',\n               'is_red_flg': 'Read as not red (used only for outcomes)',\n               'is_yellow_flg': 'Read as not yellow (used only for outcomes)',\n               'assessment_dt_wid': 'No date: outside every window, so not used'}\ncolumns = TEXT + NUMBERS + LANES\nblank = eda.select([F.avg(F.col(c).isNull().cast('double')).alias(c) for c in columns]).first().asDict()\nzero = eda.select([F.avg((F.col(c) <= 0).cast('double')).alias(c) for c in NUMBERS]).first().asDict()\nmissing = pd.DataFrame({\n    'column': columns,\n    'blank %': [round(100 * blank[c], 2) for c in columns],\n    'zero or less, % of filled rows': [round(100 * zero[c], 2) if c in zero else None for c in columns],\n    'what a blank means and what the model does': [BLANK_MEANS.get(c, '') for c in columns],\n})\nz.show(missing.sort_values('blank %', ascending=False))",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_009",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_009",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.2 Missing data by year",
      "text": "%pyspark\n# Is it getting better or worse? Blank % per year for the columns the model leans on\nWATCH = ['original_tax_amt', 'hsc_cd', 'gds_org_cty', 'supplementary_qnty', 'net_weight', 'tax_assessed', 'cpc_cd',\n         'entry_num', 'decl_status', 'clearance_station_cd']\nblank_pct = [F.round(100 * F.avg(F.col(c).isNull().cast('double')), 2).alias(c) for c in WATCH]\nz.show(eda.groupBy(F.substring('assessment_dt_wid', 1, 4).alias('year')).agg(*blank_pct).orderBy('year'))",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
