    },
    {
      "title": "2.3 Duplicates",
      "text": "%md\n## 2.3 Duplicates\n\nThe same thing can appear more than once at four levels: the same row copied, the same item repeated, the same\nentry under more than one declaration ID, and one declaration ID carrying more than one taxpayer or date. The\ntable counts each. If the copies of an item are all identical, keeping one copy loses nothing (rule R5).\n\n**Where the repeated items come from.** The view's definition joins every item to each inspection action recorded on\nits declaration (table `awunadm.insp_act_tab_t`). An item on a declaration with 40 inspection actions appears 40\ntimes. The copies differ only in the inspection columns, which the model does not use, so keeping one copy of each\nitem (R5) loses nothing. The last paragraph of this section checks this against the view.",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_012",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_012",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.3 Duplicates",
      "text": "%pyspark\nn_rows = eda.count()\nn_distinct_rows = eda.distinct().count()\nn_items = eda.select('instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr').distinct().count()\nitem_versions = eda.distinct().groupBy('instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr').count()          # different versions of an item\ncopies = eda.groupBy('instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr').count()                             # copies of an item\nids_per_entry = eda.groupBy('entry_key').agg(F.countDistinct('instance_id').alias('ids'))\nper_id = eda.groupBy('instance_id').agg(F.countDistinct('taxpayer_tin').alias('tins'),\n                                        F.countDistinct('assessment_dt_wid').alias('dates'))\nduplicates = pd.DataFrame([\n    ('Item rows (24 months, IM4 and IM7)', n_rows, ''),\n    ('Rows that are an exact copy of another row', n_rows - n_distinct_rows, 'R5 keeps one copy'),\n    ('Rows that repeat an item (same declaration ID and item number)', n_rows - n_items, 'E02, R5'),\n    ('Items whose copies are NOT all identical', item_versions.where('count > 1').count(),\n     '0 means keeping one copy loses nothing'),\n    ('Most copies of one item', copies.agg(F.max('count')).first()[0], ''),\n    ('Entries under more than one declaration ID', ids_per_entry.where('ids > 1').count(), 'E01, R14'),\n    ('Declaration IDs with more than one TIN', per_id.where('tins > 1').count(), 'expected 0'),\n    ('Declaration IDs with more than one assessment date', per_id.where('dates > 1').count(), 'expected 0'),\n], columns=['check', 'count', 'note'])\nz.show(duplicates)",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
