      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.7 The data problems",
      "text": "%md\n## 2.7 The data problems found\n\n| Issue | What we saw | What the model does |\n|---|---|---|\n| **E01** Same entry under more than one declaration ID | Entry number + station + year identifies an entry. Some entries appear under two or more declaration IDs (instance_id). | R14: the entry key is used and only the latest (highest) declaration ID of each entry is kept. Please confirm which version is the real one. |\n| **E02** The same item row repeated | The same declaration and item number appear many times (up to 522 copies). The view joins every item to each inspection action recorded on its declaration (awunadm.insp_act_tab_t), so an item appears once per action. Apart from the inspection columns, the copies are identical. | R5: each item is kept once. |\n| **E03** TIN blank or not 10 digits | Valid TINs are 10 digits. A few IM4/IM7 declarations carry a short or malformed TIN. | R1: only 10-digit TINs are scored. |\n| **E04** Cancelled declarations | Declarations with status Cancelled. | R3: cancelled declarations are left out. |\n| **E05** APC 483 (destroyed or abandoned goods, dummy reconciliation entries) | The CPC memo describes APC 483 as destroyed or abandoned goods and dummy reconciliation entries, not trade. | R13: declarations under APC 483 are left out. |\n| **E06** Top-up flag Y, but the final tax is not above the original tax | The top-up flag is set, yet the tax did not rise. | R7: a top-up counts only when the flag is Y AND the final tax is above the original tax. |\n| **E07** Tax rose, but no top-up flag | About 3,000 amended declarations have a higher final tax but no top-up flag. | Decision 18: not counted as top-ups (the flag is customs' own marking). Please confirm whether these are top-ups. |\n| **E08** Original tax blank | Original tax is blank on many declarations (about 37% of those without a top-up). | Blank is read as \"unchanged\": the final tax is used. This is our inference, not stated in the data. |\n| **E09** top_up_amt holds the final tax on declarations without a top-up | On declarations without a top-up flag, the top_up_amt column equals the final tax 99.5% of the time. | R7: top_up_amt is not used; top-up = final tax minus original tax. |\n| **E11** Value or weight zero, negative or missing | A few items have no customs value or no weight. | R8: such items are left out of the price features (they still count as declarations). |\n\nFor each problem the next paragraph collects **every item row of the entries affected**, with entry, taxpayer,\ngoods, tax, lane and status columns, so the Risk Officers can say whether it is a real data problem or how the\nsystem works. Two problems touch very many entries (E08, E09), so their tables keep a random 1 in 50 of the\nentries; the summary says so. The tables are named after the problem, for example `ctrp_eda_e01`.",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_021",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_021",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.8 Problem checks",
      "text": "%pyspark\n# Every column the officers need to judge an entry, in the order of the officer workbooks\nDETAIL = ['entry_key', 'entry_num', 'clearance_station_cd', 'dec_ref_yer', 'instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr',\n          'assessment_dt_wid', 'taxpayer_tin', 'taxpayer_nm', 'consignee_tin', 'consignee_nm', 'regime_cd',\n          'extended_proc_cd', 'cpc_cd', 'decl_status', 'hsc_cd', 'gds_org_cty', 'customs_value',\n          'net_weight', 'supplementary_qnty', 'tax_assessed', 'original_tax_amt', 'final_amt', 'top_up_amt',\n          'top_up_flg', 'amendment_flg', 'is_red_flg', 'is_yellow_flg', 'pay_status',\n          'preferential_treatment_flag']\neda_rows = eda.select(*DETAIL)\n\ndef rows_of(selected, key='instance_id'):\n    # Every item row of the declarations (or entries) in `selected`\n    return eda_rows.join(selected.select(key).distinct(), key, 'left_semi').select(*DETAIL)\n\n# One row per declaration, for the tax and lane checks\neda_decl = (eda_rows.groupBy('entry_key', 'instance_id')\n                    .agg(F.max('top_up_flg').alias('flag'),\n                         F.max('original_tax_amt').alias('orig_raw'),\n                         F.max('final_amt').alias('fin'),\n                         F.max('top_up_amt').alias('top_up_amt_max'),\n                         F.max('is_red_flg').alias('red'),\n                         F.max('is_yellow_flg').alias('yellow'))\n                    .withColumn('orig', F.coalesce('orig_raw', 'fin'))\n                    .cache())\nflag, fin, orig_raw = F.col('flag'), F.col('fin'), F.col('orig_raw')\nnot_flagged = F.coalesce(flag, F.lit('N')) != 'Y'\n\ndef e01():\n    ids = (eda_rows.groupBy('entry_key').agg(F.countDistinct('instance_id').alias('declaration_ids_on_entry'))\n                   .where('declaration_ids_on_entry > 1'))\n    return ids.join(eda_rows, 'entry_key').select('declaration_ids_on_entry', *DETAIL)\n\ndef e02():\n    copies = (eda_rows.groupBy('instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr').agg(F.count('*').alias('copies_of_item'))\n                      .where('copies_of_item > 1'))\n    return copies.join(eda_rows, ['instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr']).select('copies_of_item', *DETAIL)\n\ndef e03():\n    return eda_rows.where(~F.coalesce(F.col('taxpayer_tin'), F.lit('')).rlike('^[0-9]{10}$'))\n\ndef e04():\n    return rows_of(eda_rows.where(F.col('decl_status') == 'Cancelled'))\n\ndef e05():\n    return rows_of(eda_rows.where(F.col('cpc_cd') == '483'))\n\ndef e06():\n    return rows_of(eda_decl.where((flag == 'Y') & ~(fin > F.col('orig'))))\n\ndef e07():\n    return rows_of(eda_decl.where(not_flagged & orig_raw.isNotNull() & (fin > orig_raw)))\n\ndef e08():\n    return rows_of(eda_decl.where(orig_raw.isNull()))\n\ndef e09():\n    return rows_of(eda_decl.where(not_flagged & (F.col('top_up_amt_max') == fin) & (fin > 0)))\n\ndef e11():\n    no_value = F.coalesce('customs_value', F.lit(0)) <= 0\n    no_weight = F.coalesce('net_weight', F.lit(0)) <= 0\n    return rows_of(eda_rows.where(no_value | no_weight))\n\n# (code, title, check, keep 1 in K of the entries)\nISSUES = [\n    ('E01', 'Same entry under more than one declaration ID', e01, 1),\n    ('E02', 'The same item row repeated', e02, 1),\n    ('E03', 'TIN blank or not 10 digits', e03, 1),\n    ('E04', 'Cancelled declarations', e04, 1),\n    ('E05', 'APC 483 (destroyed or abandoned goods, dummy reconciliation entries)', e05, 1),\n    ('E06', 'Top-up flag Y, but the final tax is not above the original tax', e06, 1),\n    ('E07', 'Tax rose, but no top-up flag', e07, 1),\n    ('E08', 'Original tax blank', e08, 50),\n    ('E09', 'top_up_amt holds the final tax on declarations without a top-up', e09, 50),\n    ('E11', 'Value or weight zero, negative or missing', e11, 1),\n]\n\ndef sample(df, k):\n    # A random 1 in k of the entries (all rows of each entry kept), when a problem touches too many to read\n    return df if k == 1 else df.where(F.pmod(F.hash('entry_key'), k) == 0)\n\nprint('%d problem checks defined' % len(ISSUES))",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_022",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_022",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "2.9 Run the checks",
      "text": "%pyspark\nsummary = []\nfor code, title, check, k in ISSUES:\n    found = sample(check(), k).cache()\n    n_found, n_rows = found.select('entry_key').distinct().count(), found.count()\n    save(found, 'ctrp_eda_' + code.lower())\n    summary.append((code, title, n_found, n_rows, k))\n    print('%s  %-70s %10s %s  %10s rows' % (code, title[:70], format(n_found, ','),\n                                           'entries ', format(n_rows, ',')))\n\neda_summary = pd.DataFrame(summary, columns=['issue', 'title', 'entries_or_taxpayers', 'rows', 'sample_1_in'])\nsave(eda_summary, 'ctrp_eda_summary')\nz.show(eda_summary)",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
