    },
    {
      "title": "2.11 What the EDA tells us",
      "text": "%md\n### What the EDA tells us\n\n* Items repeat because the view joins each item to every inspection action on its declaration, so each item must be\n  kept **once** before anything is counted (E02).\n* Some entries sit under more than one declaration ID: one declaration per entry is kept (E01).\n* Cancelled declarations, invalid TINs and APC 483 are not trade and must go (E03, E04, E05).\n* Motor vehicles have their own model, so declarations with vehicles or their parts are left out.\n* Values and weights span many orders of magnitude: comparisons must be **ratios** (price per kg against other\n  importers), not raw amounts (2.2).\n* Tax amounts sit on every item row of a declaration, so taxes are taken **once per declaration**.\n* The top-up flag alone is not enough (E06), and `top_up_amt` holds the final tax on unflagged declarations (E09):\n  a top-up is the flag **and** a rise in tax, measured as final tax minus original tax.\n* Original tax is often blank when nothing changed (E08), so blank means \"same as the final tax\".",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_025",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_025",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Clean",
      "text": "%md\n## 3. Clean the rows\n\nEach rule is a yes or no question asked of every row. A row is kept only if it passes every rule. The log shows\nhow many rows each rule removed, in order.\n\n| Rule | Keeps | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | TINs of 10 digits | a TIN identifies the taxpayer (E03) |\n| R3 | declarations not cancelled | cancelled declarations are not trade (E04) |\n| R4 | regimes IM4 (home use) and IM7 (bond) | the model is about imports |\n| R13 | everything except APC 483 | destroyed or abandoned goods, dummy entries (E05) |\n| R14 | the latest declaration ID of each entry | one entry, one declaration (E01) |\n| R15 | declarations with no motor vehicle item (HS 8701, 8702, 8703, 8704, 8705, 8706, 8707, 8708, 8711) | separate motor vehicle model. The whole declaration goes, because tax and top-ups are recorded per declaration |\n| R5 | each item once | the view repeats items (E02) |",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": true,
          "completionSupport": false
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": false,
        "editorHide": true,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_026",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_026",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "3.1 Apply the rules",
      "text": "%pyspark\ndef passes(condition):\n    # A rule as a yes or no column (a blank answer counts as no)\n    return F.coalesce(condition, F.lit(False))\n\ndef removed_by_rule(df, rules):\n    # How many rows each rule removes, counting a row only at the first rule it fails\n    passed_so_far, counts = F.lit(True), []\n    for code, _ in rules:\n        counts.append(F.sum((passed_so_far & ~F.col(code)).cast('int')).alias(code))\n        passed_so_far = passed_so_far & F.col(code)\n    return df.select(counts).first().asDict()\n\n# Step 1: rules about one row at a time\nROW_RULES = [\n    ('R1', 'TIN must be 10 digits', F.col('taxpayer_tin').rlike('^[0-9]{10}$')),\n    ('R3', 'drop cancelled declarations', F.col('decl_status') != 'Cancelled'),\n    ('R4', 'imports only: IM4 (home use) and IM7 (bond)', F.col('regime_cd').isin('IM4', 'IM7')),\n    ('R13', 'drop APC 483', (F.coalesce(F.col('cpc_cd'), F.lit('')) != '483') if EXCLUDE_APC_483 else F.lit(True)),\n]\nstep1 = rows.select('*', *[passes(test).alias(code) for code, _, test in ROW_RULES])\nremoved1 = removed_by_rule(step1, [(c, t) for c, t, _ in ROW_RULES])\nrow_rule_codes = [c for c, _, _ in ROW_RULES]\nkept1 = step1.where(reduce(lambda a, b: a & b, [F.col(c) for c in row_rule_codes])).drop(*row_rule_codes)\n\n# Step 2: rules that look at the other rows of the same entry, declaration or item\npadded_id = F.lpad('instance_id', 20, '0')                      # so '99' does not sort above '100'\nlatest_id_of_entry = F.max(padded_id).over(Window.partitionBy('entry_key'))\nis_vehicle = F.substring('hsc_cd', 1, 4).isin(MOTOR_VEHICLE_HEADINGS)\ndeclaration_has_vehicle = F.max(F.when(is_vehicle, 1).otherwise(0)).over(Window.partitionBy('instance_id'))\ncopy_number = F.row_number().over(Window.partitionBy('instance_id', 'key_itm_nbr').orderBy('assessment_dt_wid'))\nSET_RULES = [\n    ('R14', 'latest declaration ID per entry',\n     (padded_id == latest_id_of_entry) if LATEST_DECLARATION_PER_ENTRY else F.lit(True)),\n    ('R15', 'drop motor vehicle declarations',\n     (declaration_has_vehicle == 0) if EXCLUDE_MOTOR_VEHICLES else F.lit(True)),\n    ('R5', 'keep each item once', copy_number == 1),\n]\nstep2 = kept1.select('*', *[passes(test).alias(code) for code, _, test in SET_RULES]).cache()\nremoved2 = removed_by_rule(step2, [(c, t) for c, t, _ in SET_RULES])\nitems = step2.where(F.col('R14') & F.col('R15') & F.col('R5')).drop('R14', 'R15', 'R5').cache()\nn_items = items.count()\nstep2.unpersist()\n\n# The cleaning log\nlog, left = [], n_loaded\nfor code, text, _ in ROW_RULES + SET_RULES:\n    gone = {**removed1, **removed2}[code]\n    log.append((code, text, left, gone, left - gone))\n    left -= gone\nassert left == n_items, 'the log does not add up'\ncleaning_log = pd.DataFrame(log, columns=['rule', 'what it does', 'rows before', 'rows removed', 'rows left'])\nsave(cleaning_log, 'ctrp_cleaning_log')\nz.show(cleaning_log)",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
        "results": {},
        "enabled": true
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "apps": [],
      "runtimeInfos": {},
      "progressUpdateIntervalMs": 500,
      "jobName": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_027",
      "id": "paragraph_ctrp_eda_027",
      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "3.2 After cleaning",
      "text": "%pyspark\nprint('Clean item rows: {:,}   declarations: {:,}   taxpayers: {:,}'.format(\n    n_items, items.select('instance_id').distinct().count(), items.select('taxpayer_tin').distinct().count()))",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
        "editorSetting": {
          "language": "python",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionSupport": true
        },
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/python",
        "colWidth": 12.0,
        "fontSize": 9.0,
        "title": true,
        "editorHide": false,
