      "dateCreated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
      "status": "READY"
    },
    {
      "title": "8.3 Check",
      "text": "%md\n### 8.3 Do these numbers match production?\n\nProduction builds the same columns with one query (`sql/live_<date>.sql`, or the \"CTRP extracts\" note). If that\nextract is in this session (a table named like `live_2026_09_30` or `bt_2026_03_31`) or saved as a table\n(`PRODUCTION_TABLE` in Settings), each column is compared, taxpayer by taxpayer. Every column should match,\nbecause both use the same rules on the same data. Differences under 0.00001 count as a match: when Spark runs the\nproduction query it rounds some rates to 5 decimal places. Larger differences can come from rows changed in the\nview since the extract was pulled (a payment made, a top-up raised later).",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20 00:00:00.000",
